{"type":"new","contents":"import Mathlib\nimport InfoGeometry.Canonical.HestenesAnalyticity\nimport InfoGeometry.Meta.Architecture\n\nopen scoped InnerProductSpace\n\nnoncomputable section\n\nnamespace InfoGeometry.Canonical.CartanInfinitesimalExponentialBridge\n\nopen InfoGeometry.Canonical.HestenesAnalyticity\nopen InfoGeometry.Krein\n\n/-!\n# Cartan Infinitesimal / Exponential Bridge\n\nThe theorem-safe translation is:\n\n* infinitesimal Cartan law: `ad_H X = [H,X] = λ • X`;\n* exponential adjoint readout: `Φ_t X = exp(tH) X exp(-tH) = exp(tλ) • X`.\n\nThe integration step is witness-gated.  This file does not prove analytic ODE\nexistence, uniqueness, or noncommutative exponential calculus.\n-/\n\n/-! ## 1. Generic algebraic Cartan derivation -/\n\nsection Algebraic\n\nvariable {R : Type*}\nvariable [Ring R] [Algebra ℝ R]\n\n/-- Cartan/adjoint derivation `ad_H(X) = H X - X H`. -/\n@[rep_depth operator]\ndef cartanAdjoint (H X : R) : R :=\n  H * X - X * H\n\n/-- `X` is an eigen-operator of the Cartan derivation generated by `H`. -/\n@[rep_depth operator]\ndef IsCartanEigenOperator (H X : R) (lam : ℝ) : Prop :=\n  cartanAdjoint H X = lam • X\n\n/-- Readback: the infinitesimal law is exactly `ad_H(X)=λX`. -/\n@[rep_depth operator]\ntheorem cartanEigenOperator_readback\n    {H X : R} {lam : ℝ}\n    (hX : IsCartanEigenOperator H X lam) :\n    H * X - X * H = lam • X :=\n  hX\n\n/-- The generator commutes with itself, so it has weight zero under its own adjoint action. -/\n@[rep_depth operator]\ntheorem cartanAdjoint_self_zero\n    (H : R) :\n    cartanAdjoint H H = 0 := by\n  simp [cartanAdjoint]\n\n/--\nCartan weights are preserved by conjugating the whole frame.\n\nIf `H₂ = U H₁ U⁻¹` and `U⁻¹U=1`, then an eigen-operator `X`\nof `ad_{H₁}` with weight `λ` transports to `U X U⁻¹`, still with weight `λ`.\n-/\n@[rep_depth operator]\ntheorem cartanEigenOperator_conjugate\n    {H₁ H₂ X U Uinv : R} {lam : ℝ}\n    (hH : H₂ = U * H₁ * Uinv)\n    (hL : Uinv * U = 1)\n    (hX : IsCartanEigenOperator H₁ X lam) :\n    IsCartanEigenOperator H₂ (U * X * Uinv) lam := by\n  unfold IsCartanEigenOperator cartanAdjoint at hX ⊢\n  rw [hH]\n  calc\n    (U * H₁ * Uinv) * (U * X * Uinv) -\n        (U * X * Uinv) * (U * H₁ * Uinv)\n        =\n      U * H₁ * (Uinv * U) * X * Uinv -\n        U * X * (Uinv * U) * H₁ * Uinv := by\n          noncomm_ring\n    _ =\n      U * H₁ * 1 * X * Uinv -\n        U * X * 1 * H₁ * Uinv := by\n          rw [hL]\n    _ =\n      U * (H₁ * X - X * H₁) * Uinv := by\n          noncomm_ring\n    _ =\n      U * (lam • X) * Uinv := by\n          rw [hX]\n    _ =\n      lam • (U * X * Uinv) := by\n          simp [Algebra.smul_mul_assoc, Algebra.mul_smul_comm, mul_assoc]\n\nend Algebraic\n\n/-! ## 2. Exponential-flow calibration socket -/\n\nsection ExponentialFlow\n\nvariable {V : Type*}\nvariable [AddCommGroup V] [Module ℝ V]\n\n/--\nA supplied exponential eigen-flow.\n\n`flow_law` is the integrated calibration `Φ_t(X) = exp(tλ) X`.\nThis is a socket, not an analytic ODE theorem.\n-/\n@[rep_depth operator]\nstructure ExponentialEigenFlow where\n  flow : ℝ → V → V\n  eigenvector : V\n  eigenvalue : ℝ\n  /-- Integrated eigen-flow readout. -/\n  flow_law :\n    ∀ t : ℝ, flow t eigenvector = Real.exp (t * eigenvalue) • eigenvector\n\nnamespace ExponentialEigenFlow\n\nvariable (F : ExponentialEigenFlow (V := V))\n\n/-- At time zero, the exponential eigen-flow fixes the eigenvector. -/\n@[rep_depth operator]\ntheorem flow_zero_on_eigenvector :\n    F.flow 0 F.eigenvector = F.eigenvector := by\n  rw [F.flow_law 0]\n  simp\n\n/-- Additive time readback on the eigenvector: `Φ_{t+s}(X) = exp(tλ) Φ_s(X)`. -/\n@[rep_depth operator]\ntheorem flow_add_on_eigenvector\n    (t s : ℝ) :\n    F.flow (t + s) F.eigenvector =\n      Real.exp (t * F.eigenvalue) • F.flow s F.eigenvector := by\n  calc\n    F.flow (t + s) F.eigenvector\n        = Real.exp ((t + s) * F.eigenvalue) • F.eigenvector := by\n            rw [F.flow_law (t + s)]\n    _ = Real.exp (t * F.eigenvalue + s * F.eigenvalue) • F.eigenvector := by\n            have harg :\n                (t + s) * F.eigenvalue =\n                  t * F.eigenvalue + s * F.eigenvalue := by\n              ring\n            rw [harg]\n    _ = (Real.exp (t * F.eigenvalue) * Real.exp (s * F.eigenvalue)) •\n          F.eigenvector := by\n            rw [Real.exp_add]\n    _ = Real.exp (t * F.eigenvalue) •\n          (Real.exp (s * F.eigenvalue) • F.eigenvector) := by\n            rw [smul_smul]\n    _ = Real.exp (t * F.eigenvalue) • F.flow s F.eigenvector := by\n            rw [F.flow_law s]\n\nend ExponentialEigenFlow\n\nend ExponentialFlow\n\n/-! ## 3. Inner adjoint exponential-flow calibration -/\n\nsection InnerAdjoint\n\nvariable {R : Type*}\nvariable [Ring R] [Algebra ℝ R]\n\n/--\nA Cartan eigen-operator with a supplied inner exponential-adjoint transport law.\n\nThe maps `expH` and `expNegH` are carried abstractly.  This file does not\nconstruct them from a functional calculus.\n-/\n@[rep_depth operator]\nstructure CartanEigenAdjointExponentialCalibration where\n  H : R\n  X : R\n  weight : ℝ\n  /-- Abstract `exp(tH)` carrier. -/\n  expH : ℝ → R\n  /-- Abstract `exp(-tH)` carrier. -/\n  expNegH : ℝ → R\n  /-- Infinitesimal Cartan eigen-operator law `[H,X]=λX`. -/\n  infinitesimal_law :\n    IsCartanEigenOperator H X weight\n  /-- Integrated exponential-adjoint law. -/\n  exponential_adjoint_law :\n    ∀ t : ℝ, expH t * X * expNegH t = Real.exp (t * weight) • X\n\nnamespace CartanEigenAdjointExponentialCalibration\n\nvariable (C : CartanEigenAdjointExponentialCalibration (R := R))\n\n/-- Readback of the infinitesimal law. -/\n@[rep_depth operator]\ntheorem infinitesimal_readback :\n    cartanAdjoint C.H C.X = C.weight • C.X :=\n  C.infinitesimal_law\n\n/-- Readback of the supplied exponential-adjoint law. -/\n@[rep_depth operator]\ntheorem exponential_adjoint_readback\n    (t : ℝ) :\n    C.expH t * C.X * C.expNegH t = Real.exp (t * C.weight) • C.X :=\n  C.exponential_adjoint_law t\n\n/-- At time zero, if the exponential carriers act as identities, the readout fixes `X`. -/\n@[rep_depth operator]\ntheorem exponential_zero_readback\n    (hpos : C.expH 0 = 1)\n    (hneg : C.expNegH 0 = 1) :\n    C.expH 0 * C.X * C.expNegH 0 = C.X := by\n  rw [hpos, hneg]\n  simp\n\nend CartanEigenAdjointExponentialCalibration\n\nend InnerAdjoint\n\n/-! ## 4. Hestenes-Krein analytic compatibility -/\n\nsection HestenesKrein\n\nvariable {E : Type 0}\nvariable [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E] [CompleteSpace E]\n\nlocal notation \"H₂\" => DoubledSpace E\nlocal notation \"EndH\" => H₂ →L[ℝ] H₂\n\n/--\nHestenes-Krein Cartan eigen-operator law using the real operator commutator on\ndoubled endomorphisms.\n-/\n@[rep_depth krein]\ndef IsHestenesCartanEigenOperator\n    (H X : EndH) (lam : ℝ) : Prop :=\n  hestenesSymmetryCommutator (E := E) H X = lam • X\n\n/--\nIf `H` and `X` preserve the internal Hestenes phase axis, then their Cartan\ncommutator also preserves it.\n-/\n@[rep_depth krein]\ntheorem hestenesCartan_commutator_is_analytic\n    {H X : EndH}\n    (hH : IsHestenesAnalyticSymmetry (E := E) H)\n    (hX : IsHestenesAnalyticSymmetry (E := E) X) :\n    IsHestenesAnalyticSymmetry (E := E)\n      (hestenesSymmetryCommutator (E := E) H X) :=\n  hestenesAnalyticSymmetry_commutator (E := E) hH hX\n\n/--\nIf `[H,X]=λX` and `H,X` are Hestenes analytic, then the eigen-image `λX`\nis also Hestenes analytic.\n-/\n@[rep_depth krein]\ntheorem hestenesCartan_eigen_image_is_analytic\n    {H X : EndH} {lam : ℝ}\n    (hEig : IsHestenesCartanEigenOperator (E := E) H X lam)\n    (hH : IsHestenesAnalyticSymmetry (E := E) H)\n    (hX : IsHestenesAnalyticSymmetry (E := E) X) :\n    IsHestenesAnalyticSymmetry (E := E) (lam • X) := by\n  rw [← hEig]\n  exact hestenesCartan_commutator_is_analytic (E := E) hH hX\n\nend HestenesKrein\n\nend InfoGeometry.Canonical.CartanInfinitesimalExponentialBridge\n","mtime":1778732248702}